While qjs-ng added support for `atob` and `btoa` in commit [#b1a0410](https://github.com/quickjs-ng/quickjs/commit/b1a04105245b2913af970ad9e4af73a4e4bc2394), LLRT had a Rust implementation earlier, so this functionality is hidden within the Rust implementation and not enabled.

~To verify the performance level, we enabled only the global implementation and obtained benchmark results, which showed approximately 2-3x the performance.~
When I prepared several strings of different lengths and ran the test repeatedly, there wasn't much difference in performance between the two implementations.

<details>
  <summary>benchmark</summary>

```javascript
// atobtoa.js
import { run, bench, group, summary } from 'mitata';

import { atob as _atob, btoa as _btoa } from 'buffer'; // rust implimentation

[
  ["small", "dXNlcjpwYXNz"],
  ["middle", "aGVsbG8gd29ybGQgdGhpcyBpcyBhIGxvbmdlciBiYXNlNjQgc3RyaW5nIGZvciB0ZXN0aW5n"],
  ["large", "VGhpcyBpcyBhIGxvbmcgYmFzZTY0IHN0cmluZyBleGFtcGxlIHRoYXQgcmVwcmVzZW50cyBhIGxhcmdlciBwYXlsb2FkLiBUaGlzIGlzIHVzZWQgdG8gc2ltdWxhdGUgYSBiaWdnZXIgZGF0YSBibG9iIGluIGEgcmVhbGlzdGljIHNjZW5hcmlvLg=="],
].forEach(([type, input]) => {
  group('atob: ' + type, () => {
    summary(() => {
      bench('qjs', () => {
        atob(input);
      })
      bench('llrt', () => {
        _atob(input);
      })
    });
  });
});

[
  ["small", "hello world"],
  ["middle", "hello world this is a longer buffer example for iteration testing"],
  ["large", "hello world this is a longer buffer example for iteration testing, hello world this is a longer buffer example for iteration testing"],
].forEach(([type, input]) => {
  group('btoa: ' + type, () => {
    summary(() => {
      bench('qjs', () => {
        btoa(input);
      })
      bench('llrt', () => {
        _btoa(input);
      })
    });
  });
});

await run();
```

