According to the documentation, you should be using `response.Body.transformToString` to get the response.  It seems that body is actually a Uint8Array so transformToString doesn't exist. 

The logic/data does work if you use a TextDecoder.  But the documentation doesn't seem to match the current documentation on the front page.

Below is the current code I use for working around this:

```
export const transformToString = async (
  response: GetObjectCommandOutput | { Body: Uint8Array },
): Promise<string> => {
  const { Body } = response;

  if (Body instanceof Uint8Array) {
    return decoder.decode(Body);
  } else {
    return await Body?.transformToString() ?? "{}";
  }
};
```

