### Issue Title
Lambda to DynamoDB Local Connection Issue with `@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb`: Invalid Authority Error

### Description
I am encountering a problem when attempting to connect to DynamoDB Local from a Lambda function using the `amazon/aws-lambda-provided:al2023` runtime. I performed three different tests to establish a connection and interact with DynamoDB Local. These tests were designed to compare the behavior of direct HTTP requests using `fetch` with and without fake authorization headers, against using the AWS SDK (`@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb`).

### Test 1: Direct HTTP Request without Authorization (Using `fetch`)

```javascript
try {
  const date = new Date().toISOString();
  const response = await fetch('http://dynamodb-local:8000', {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": "application/x-amz-json-1.0",
      "X-Amz-Target": "DynamoDB_20120810.ListTables",
      "X-Amz-Date": date.replace(/[:-]|\.\d{3}/g, ""),
    },
    body: "{}",
  });
  const data = await response.json();
  console.log("Respuesta:", data);
} catch (error) {
  console.error("Error al realizar la solicitud a DynamoDB:", error.message || error);
}
```

This resulted in the following error:

```
{"__type":"com.amazonaws.dynamodb.v20120810#MissingAuthenticationToken","Message":"Request must contain either a valid (registered) AWS access key ID or X.509 certificate."}
```

### Test 2: Direct HTTP Request with Fake Authorization (Using `fetch`)

```javascript
try {
  const date = new Date().toISOString();
  const response = await fetch('http://dynamodb-local:8000', {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": "application/x-amz-json-1.0",
      "X-Amz-Target": "DynamoDB_20120810.ListTables",
      "X-Amz-Date": date.replace(/[:-]|\.\d{3}/g, ""),
      Authorization: `AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential=${config.credentials.accessKeyId}/${awsDate}/us-west-2/dynamodb/aws4_request, SignedHeaders=content-type;host;x-amz-date;x-amz-target, Signature=fakeSignature`,
    },
    body: "{}",
  });
  const data = await response.json();
  console.log("Respuesta:", data);
} catch (error) {
  console.error("Error al realizar la solicitud a DynamoDB:", error.message || error);
}
```

This provided the correct response:

```
{"TableNames":["test"]}
```

### Test 3: Using `@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb`

```javascript
const config = {
  region: "us-west-2",
  endpoint: "http://dynamodb-local:8000",
  credentials: {
    accessKeyId: "yourAccessKeyId",
    secretAccessKey: "yourSecretAccessKey",
    sessionToken: "yourSessionToken",
  },
};

const client = new DynamoDBClient(config);

try {
  const command = new ListTablesCommand({});
  const response = await client.send(command);
  const data = response.TableNames;
  console.log("TableNames:", data);
} catch (error) {
  console.error("Error:", error.message);
}
```

This attempt resulted in the following error:

```
"invalid authority"
```

### Conclusion
The direct HTTP requests using `fetch` demonstrate that the DynamoDB Local can be accessed and queried with proper headers, even with fake credentials. However, when attempting to use the `@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb` for the same purpose, an "invalid authority" error occurs. This suggests a specific issue with how `@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb` is handling requests to DynamoDB Local.

### Additional Information
- Lambda runtime: `amazon/aws-lambda-provided:al2023`
- DynamoDB Local is accessed through `http://dynamodb-local:8000`

### Request for Help
I am seeking assistance or insights from anyone who might have encountered similar issues or has suggestions on how to resolve the "invalid authority" error with `@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb`. Any advice or guidance would be highly appreciated.

PS: This issue has been translated by ChatGPT as my primary language is Spanish 😃 😘 

### Update 1

I've made progress in my investigation and setup, which includes adjustments to my project configuration and code. Here's a detailed overview:

#### `package.json` Configuration
```json
{
  "name": "proyecto-lambda-dynamodb-crud",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Proyecto para testear DynamoDB Local",
  "type": "module",
  "main": "index.js",
  "scripts": {
    "build": "tsc",
    "start": "npm run build && node dist/index.js",
    "dev": "tsc",
    "npm:reinstall": "rm -rf node_modules && rm -rf dist && rm -f package-lock.json && npm cache clean --force && npm install"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb": "^3.521.0",
    "@aws-sdk/util-dynamodb": "^3.521.0",
    "@types/aws-lambda": "^8.10.134",
    "@types/node": "^20.11.20",
    "typescript": "^5.3.3"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "aws-lambda": "^1.0.7",
    "aws-sdk": "^2.1566.0"
  }
}
```

#### File: `index.ts`
```typescript
